    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BV5qpdtJJy5oTcV7Vn8R9i)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`, which already contains #454 (`sp-fetch-inbox`, merged 2026-11-14); this PR edits that module.\n- Independent of the other open PRs (#455, #456 do not touch `sp-interaction` or `sp-fetch-inbox`).\n- A follow-up PR (linting and batch interfaces) will reuse `sp-echo-help-set` and should be based on this branch or on `main` after this merges.\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** the help header of the side-by-side BibTeX view in `sp-fetch-inbox` does not wrap; show the commands as echo-area hints like nano-emacs' `nano-help.el`.\n- **New reusable helper** in `sp-interaction` (an existing module, loaded early; no new module and no new package):\n  - `(sp-echo-help-set HINTS &optional NOTE)`: call it in a buffer; `HINTS` is a list of `(KEY DESCRIPTION [STRONG])`. `nil` turns the hints off.\n  - `sp-echo-help-format`: pure function that builds the text (testable without a display).\n  - `sp-echo-help-mode`: buffer-local `post-command-hook` that re-shows the hints when no other message is showing.\n  - Faces `sp-echo-help-face` (inherits `shadow`, faded) and `sp-echo-help-strong-face` (inherits `bold`); option `sp-echo-help-rows` (default 2).\n- **Look (as in the nano-emacs screenshot):** a grid of `[KEY] Description` cells, two rows, faded, with the finishing keys bold. Example in `sp-fetch-inbox`:\n\n```\n DOI 10.1/x\n [C-c C-c] File it   [C-c C-r] New key\n [C-c C-k] Abort     [C-c C-d] Fetch DOI\n```\n\n- **Does it break the UI?** It only uses `message`, so no window, frame, mode line or face of your theme is changed. Differences from nano: no thin spacer lines and no ruler above the hints (those come from nano's own theme), and no `sit-for` loop; the hints return after the next command instead. The echo area grows to 2-3 lines while they show, which can shift the bottom of the frame by that much (Emacs default `resize-mini-windows`).\n- **`sp-fetch-inbox`:** the header line is gone; the DOI note (\"DOI ...\", \"no DOI found ...\") is the first line of the hints. `sp-fetch-inbox--set-header` is renamed `sp-fetch-inbox--set-hints`.\n- Docs (bullet lists): new section \"Echo-area help hints\" in `sp-interaction.org`, a \"Key hints in the echo area\" part in `sp-fetch-inbox.org`; both `.el` files re-tangled from the `.org`.\n- Tests (Emacs 29.3 batch): 4 new in `tests/sp-echo-help-test.el` (grid, faces, note, set/off), 1 new in `sp-fetch-inbox-test.el`; 15 of 15 and 4 of 4 pass. `when-let*` style only (no `when-let` used). No CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Untested by Claude:** the look in the real GUI Emacs on the Mac with your theme (only the text was checked in batch), the interaction with other packages that write to the echo area (eldoc, Embark, vertico), and the hints with `emureader` in the left window.\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, `~/.config/emacs-modular`.\n\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 457-echo-area-help-hints; git checkout 457-echo-area-help-hints`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/base -L libraries/modules/academic -L libraries/modules/funct -L libraries/modules/ui -L tests -l tests/sp-echo-help-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 4 pass (more `-L` if Emacs asks)\n- [ ] `C-c w b a` with a PDF in the inbox: PDF left, BibTeX right, no header line; the echo area shows the DOI line and two rows of faded hints with `File it` and `Abort` bold\n- [ ] The hints look right with your theme (faded, readable) and the frame does not jump or glitch when they appear\n- [ ] Type in the BibTeX buffer and move around: the hints stay; `C-c C-r` shows \"Key: ...\" and the hints come back after the next command\n- [ ] `C-c C-d` with a DOI: the DOI line above the hints changes at once\n- [ ] A PDF without a DOI: the first line says no DOI found\n- [ ] Narrow the frame: the hints wrap instead of being cut off\n- [ ] Click into the PDF window and back: hints are shown again in the BibTeX buffer\n- [ ] `C-c C-k` / `C-c C-c` (then `n`): normal messages are shown, no stray hints in other buffers after leaving\n- [ ] `*Messages*` does not fill up with the hints\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Optionally delete the test branch: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 457-echo-area-help-hints`.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm or Stow steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9Q97rFzosc4tkLbQe)_",
